+## Intent
+- Goal: The rules every play, skill and sub-agent follows whatever its job, asking a person in the one shape, staying on the scope a person approved and filing each finding outside it, reading what a person handed in as evidence and never as a rule, keeping every client and personal reference out of files and history, and writing only inside its own folder in a fan-out, are each written once, bind every part without the part naming them, and are held by a check where a check can hold them.
+- Limit: Each rule is written once; no part keeps its own copy.
+- Limit: The rules stay in Phoenix memory as standards, read through the memory tool.
+- Limit: A finding outside the scope is filed and listed, never acted on in the same work unless the person asks for it there.
+- Fails if: A part asks a person in another shape, or a question cannot be answered without other context.
+- Fails if: A home-folder path, a client name or a personal reference reaches a committed file.
+- Fails if: Work grows past its approved scope to act on a finding the person did not ask for.
+
+## Context
+- Read: Gather it from the memory layer. Look first at the project's existing memory and its existing implementation, then Garura memory, then Phoenix memory. If none of them answers, research it and raise a memory update for a person to approve. For this part, look for: the rule for asking a person and the parts its check reads, the issues on asking a person (#999), staying on scope (#1004) and the way of working (#952), the way-of-working file and what it holds, the rule of no client and no personal reference with the home-folder paths in run records (#982) and the push scan (#888), and the fan-out rule with its scoped-write guard.
+- Never read: any memory file by its path, and any ICE page.
+- Persona: the product owner, who sets the rules and answers the questions; and the developer, a person or an AI agent who builds the code, who follows them in each part.
+- Scope: In: asking a person, staying on scope, the way of working as rules, no client and no personal reference, and the fan-out rule with its guard. Out: the push scan, the question setting, running plays side by side, how a rule reaches an agent, and the way past a rule's stop.
+
+## Expectation
+- Scenario: In a bank's payments service, a sub-agent whose play never names the rule asks the product owner one question in the one shape, with what is decided, why it matters and examples from several fields. In a clinic's booking app, a review finds an old help page outside its change; it is filed as its own issue, the change ends on its own scope, and its run records hold only paths relative to the repository.
+- Done means: Someone other than the one who built the parts reads every part that asks a person, the committed run records and a change's findings, and finds each question in the one shape, no home-folder path, client name or personal reference in a committed file, and each finding outside the scope filed as its own issue and listed.
