+{
+ "by": "product-os-keeper, for #1021 (reorganise the business intents): BI-10 close, item 4",
+ "source": ".garura/project/issues/1021/context/bi-10-close/approval.md: \"Argus can only allow from short term to the project memory. Going to the Phoenix is not designed yet. That would need an organizational change. It will happen in Sphinx or Griffin that we are building, but not in Karo.\"",
+ "pages": [
+  {
+   "page": "software-delivery-planning/memory/fn-promote-page/feature.md",
+   "changes": [
+    {
+     "old": "A page moves up a tier, from an issue's short-term memory to Garura memory, or up to Phoenix memory, only when a person says yes to it in the Memory section of Argus, and what Run → Product learned is proposed there for that person to choose, so an answer one issue found can reach the next issue without anyone copying it by hand.",
+     "new": "A page moves up a tier, from an issue's short-term memory to the project's Garura memory, only when a person says yes to it in the Memory section of Argus, and what Run → Product learned is proposed there for that person to choose, so an answer one issue found can reach the next issue without anyone copying it by hand. Nothing moves from a project to Phoenix memory."
+    },
+    {
+     "old": "- A promotion moves a page up a tier. \"A person makes it on purpose, outside the work\". It is the only way Garura memory and Phoenix memory change.",
+     "new": "- A promotion moves a page up a tier. \"A person makes it on purpose, outside the work\". It is the only way a page an issue found reaches Garura memory."
+    },
+    {
+     "old": "- What may enter each tier: short-term memory takes the issue's own work and its approved updates; Garura memory takes what `initialize` builds for the project from Phoenix memory, the product model its own plays write, and a promotion a person said yes to; Phoenix memory changes only by a promotion, and takes only what is generic, with no names of a client, an organisation or a person.",
+     "new": "- What may enter each tier: short-term memory takes the issue's own work and its approved updates; Garura memory takes what `initialize` builds for the project from Phoenix memory, the product model its own plays write, and a promotion a person said yes to; Phoenix memory is not changed from a project: moving a page to it is not designed, needs an organisational change, and is to happen outside Garura."
+    },
+    {
+     "old": "- Who does what, in the product owner's answer of 2026-11-11: moving a page up and choosing what is learned are this capability's, on a person's yes; the person gives the yes in the Memory section of Argus, in Developer tooling; and Run → Product proposes what was learned.",
+     "new": "- Who does what, in the product owner's answer of 2026-11-11: moving a page up and choosing what is learned are this capability's, on a person's yes; the person gives the yes in the Memory section of Argus, in Developer tooling, for a move to Garura memory only: \"Argus can only allow from short term to the project memory.\"; and Run → Product proposes what was learned."
+    },
+    {
+     "old": "  - In an open-source library's harness, a generic rule on how to name a release has proved itself in two projects. The product owner says yes to moving it up to Phoenix memory, and it lands there as one commit.",
+     "new": "  - In a bank's payments service, a rule on how refunds are named has proved itself in one issue. The technical lead says yes to it in Argus, and it moves to the bank's Garura memory; it does not go to Phoenix memory, which no project changes."
+    },
+    {
+     "old": "- In: a page in an issue's short-term memory, such as an approved memory update or a person's answer, or a page in Garura memory.",
+     "new": "- In: a page in an issue's short-term memory, such as an approved memory update or a person's answer."
+    },
+    {
+     "old": "- Out, on a yes: the page in Garura memory, or in Phoenix memory as one commit, with a record of who said yes and their words.",
+     "new": "- Out, on a yes: the page in the project's Garura memory, with a record of who said yes and their words."
+    },
+    {
+     "old": "- Every change to Phoenix memory is a commit. The reason: \"Every change here is a commit.\"",
+     "new": "- Nothing moves from a project to Phoenix memory. The reason, in the product owner's words: \"Going to the Phoenix is not designed yet. That would need an organizational change.\""
+    },
+    {
+     "old": "- Phoenix memory takes only what is generic. The reason: \"No client, organisation or personal references.\"",
