+# BI-11 close: the proposal shown to the product owner (draft, not applied)
+
+2026-11-11. BI-11 (Product model) has its two capabilities in the model: Define what a product is made of, and Manage the model. This is the close, as for BI-4 and BI-6 to BI-10. Nothing is applied before the product owner's yes.
+
+## 1. BI-11's page (`.garura/product/product-os/intents/bi-11.md`): kept as it is
+Each part of its Outcome has a capability: "an ontology that defines what a product is made of" (Define what a product is made of), "a model defined and managed as it grows" and "a source of new ideas and experiments" (Manage the model, with Propose what to try next). Each Proof line has a feature: "A person changes the ontology through one play and the model still passes its checks." (Change the map through one play, and Run the model's checks before and after every change to the map); "Any part can be added, changed or removed." (Add, Change and Take out a part); "From any intent, you can list what serves it." (fn-726); "The model proposes an idea with its evidence, a person confirms it, and an experiment records the result." (Propose what to try next). The Must not stands.
+
+## 2. The domain: the two stay in software delivery planning
+- Added to the domain page's first paragraph, before "It does not release the work or run the product.": It also defines what a product is made of, and keeps each product's model as a living map: added to, changed and pruned as work is done, and the source of what to try next.
+
+## 3. The two capability pages that left the domain to the close
+On each: "It sits in software delivery planning with the other capability of Product model. The domain's first paragraph does not name it yet; widening it is owed at this intent's close." becomes "It sits in software delivery planning with the other capability of Product model, and the domain's first paragraph says so."; and one Sources line quoting the domain's new sentence.
+
