+- Read: Gather it from the memory layer. Look first at the project's existing memory and its existing implementation, then Garura memory, then Phoenix memory. If none of them answers, research it and raise a memory update for a person to approve. For this part, look for: the project's code and its settings, such as infrastructure files that create environments, pipeline files that name them, container and compose files, and an example settings file; the deployment design, with the path, what each environment is for and the one design every environment is built from; the approved architecture and the declared surfaces; the compliance needs in the product profile; the project's set-up answers, when it has them; Phoenix memory's architecture and technology learnings on environments, with the conditions each fits; and the environments declared so far, with the decisions behind them.
