+
+## Intent
+- Goal: Every story, chore and spike in the tree gathered under the item the technical lead names gets, before it is built, a technical part that names its classes, functions, reusable patterns and files with code samples of their shape, and a surface part that says what a person or system sees and does on its one surface, in one design made against the project's standards and confirmed by the technical lead.
+- Limit: The design starts only from the builder's part of the gathered tree and each story's collected context; it never reads the test writer's part, the evals folder, an eval, the hidden file or an ICE page, and holds no eval, test, success scenario, story expectation or failure condition.
+- Limit: The design follows the project's architecture and technology, the declared surface with its properties and guidelines, the deployment design and the environments, and never changes them; a need they do not cover is named as a gap for the capability that owns it, with what the design chose meanwhile.
+- Limit: Each choice reuses what the project's code already has before it names something new, names its source and the other ways weighed, and comes from the project's code and memory first, then Garura memory, then Phoenix memory, or from research only after a person approves it as a memory update.
+- Fails if: A story, chore or spike under the chosen item has no technical part, or no surface part and no line that says why it has none, or the design covers an item from outside the chosen item's tree.
+- Fails if: The design holds an eval, a test, a success scenario, a story's expectation or a failure condition, or names the evals folder, the hidden file or an ICE page.
+- Fails if: A choice in the design breaks a project standard, or has no source in the project, in memory or in a memory update a person approved.
+
+## Context
+- Read: Gather it from the memory layer. Look first at the project's existing memory and its existing implementation, then Garura memory, then Phoenix memory. If none of them answers, research it and raise a memory update for a person to approve. For this part, look for: the builder's part of the gathered tree and each story's collected context, the one surface the work's slice names, the project's architecture with its technology, the declared surface with its properties and guidelines such as its design system, the deployment design and the environments, the classes, functions, files and patterns already in the project's code, and the memory's learnings for that kind of surface and technology.
+- Never read: the test writer's part, the plan's evals folder, the eval, the slice's hidden file and any ICE page.
+- Persona: the technical lead, who designs the work under the chosen item with an AI agent and confirms each choice; the developer later builds from the design, test first.
+- Scope: In: the technical part and the surface part of every story, chore and spike under the chosen item, the gaps in the project's standards, the work items that do not fit, and the bugs named for their fix. Out: gathering the work, setting the project's standards, updating the design later, the tests and the code, the evals and the hidden file, a bug's fix, and the product model.
+
+## Expectation
+- Scenario: The technical lead of a team's task tool, a command a person runs in a terminal, names a story with a chore and a bug under it. The design gives the story a new function inside the project's existing task store, named with its file and shown in a short code sample, and a surface part with the command, what it prints and how a person answers; the chore gets a technical part and a line that says it has no surface because it only tidies the store's files; the bug is named for Fix defects test first. A choice of how long a task is kept, which no memory tier holds, is raised as a memory update and stays open. The technical lead confirms the design.
+- Done means: Someone other than the one who designed the work compares the design with the gathered tree and the project's standards, and finds every story, chore and spike with both parts or a reason for no surface, none from outside its tree, each choice with its source, and no standard broken.
+- Done means: Someone other than the one who designed the work searches the design and finds no expectation, eval, test, success scenario or failure condition, and no name of the evals folder, the hidden file or an ICE page.
