+## Intent
+- Goal: Each failure the eval finds goes back as a handoff plan that says what the product does wrong, as a symptom, and the way back. For a failure condition, the way back comes from the recovery parts of the slice's hidden file only, and the plan goes to the developer through Build the work test first when the recovery says the builder can fix it alone, to the product owner when a person must decide, and to Fix defects test first when the work was already accepted. For a goal or an expectation not met, the plan names that line of the story: a goal goes to the developer, an expectation only to the test writer.
+- Limit: A handoff plan never names the failure condition, its id, the scenario, its steps or the check, and its way back is guidance, never code.
+- Limit: Only the recovery parts of the hidden file are read, never its failure conditions; the recovery's who fixes decides where the plan goes.
+- Limit: A handoff plan is the whole of the work it calls for, and the verdict says where each one went.
+- Fails if: A handoff plan names a failure condition, its id, a scenario or the check, or the builder is handed an expectation of the story.
+- Fails if: A handoff plan whose recovery says a person must decide went to the developer, or one the builder can fix alone went nowhere.
+- Fails if: The failure conditions of the hidden file were read to write a handoff plan.
