+## Intent
+- Goal: A team that works in Factory's agent installs Garura and gets an install built for Factory: a Factory adapter, behind the one engine, lays each chosen part that the agent can run where the agent reads it, with Garura's instructions beside the team's own, the memory guide where every agent reads it, and every path in the install record; until that adapter exists, Factory is named as removed and an install that names it is refused before anything is written.
+- Limit: Any return of Factory goes through an adapter behind the one engine and the install record, never a sync step beside the install.
+- Limit: The adapter rests only on what Factory is and its agent loads as approved in memory, never on a guess.
+- Limit: No part is laid without what it needs to run, and no file of the team's own is written over.
+- Fails if: An install for Factory writes anything while it has no adapter, or Factory is shown as supported while it is not.
+- Fails if: After an install, a part of the kind is missing from where Factory's agent reads it, or does not load, or a laid path is not in the install record.
+- Fails if: A file of the team's own changed, or a step of the engine changed to add the tool.
+
+## Context
+- Read: Gather it from the memory layer. Look first at the project's existing memory and its existing implementation, then Garura memory, then Phoenix memory. If none of them answers, research it and raise a memory update for a person to approve. For this part, look for: which product Factory is and what its agent loads from a project, as approved in memory; what the removed sync skill did and why it was removed; the leftovers in Garura's settings file and `AGENTS.md`; the adapters already built; and the team's own files for Factory's agent.
+- Never read: any memory file by its path, and any ICE page.
+- Persona: the product owner, whose team works in Factory's agent.
+- Scope: In: Factory's state, its leftovers named, and a Factory adapter and what it lays. Out: the engine's steps, which tier each part runs on, what each guardrail guards, and changing the leftovers.
