+# BI-7 close: the proposal shown to the product owner (draft, not applied)
+
+2026-11-10. BI-7 (Install and distribute) has its four capabilities in the model: Install into a project, Upgrade a project, Support each coding tool, and Set a project up after the install (Initialize). This is the close, as for BI-4 and BI-6: BI-7's page brought in line with the four, the domain question settled, and the approved pages that left the domain to the close brought in line. Nothing is applied before the product owner's yes.
+
+## 1. BI-7's page (`.garura/product/product-os/intents/bi-7.md`)
+
+Every line of the page is quoted on approved pages (the Outcome on 1, the Why on 3, each Proof on 2, the Must not on 15), so each line stays word for word and the close only adds.
+
+- Outcome, kept: A team gets Garura into its project, upgrades it knowing what changes, and uses it on whichever coding tool it has.
+- Outcome, one sentence added after it: Once Garura is in, the project is set up from the team's own answers, with its own memory, its review rules and its tracker's work-item types, and the team can take Garura out again, keeping its work and its own files.
+- Why: kept.
+- Proof, kept: the three lines.
+- Proof, one line added after them: After the set-up, the project's own memory and its review hold only what the team's answers call for.
+- Must not: kept.
+- Stage, tracker and the 28 Touches lines: kept.
+
+## 2. The domain question: the four capabilities stay in software delivery planning
+
+- Decision proposed: all four capabilities of Install and distribute stay in software delivery planning, and the domain's first paragraph says so.
+- Why: Initialize already sat there before this review, the domain holds every part these four install, set up and keep current, and BI-6 settled the same way. The domain's name is parked for a later review; a domain of its own for Garura's own distribution can come then.
