+## Intent
+- Goal: One list names every pinned yes, today the merge onto main, confirming an intent and accepting an ADR by hand, the shaping checkpoints of /shape-slice, /shape-plan and /shape-eval and the three of /edit-ontology, each with why it is pinned, where it is asked and what happens to it inside a loop, and it agrees with the gate rule's pinned set; once #992's ADR is accepted, each carries the ADR's answer, so every reader knows which yeses no setting reaches and how each meets Orchestration's Must not.
+- Limit: No setting, policy, ledger or agent turns a pinned yes off, and only a person gives one.
+- Limit: The list takes no side on whether a typed yes is a way past or a stop kept on purpose until #992's ADR decides it.
+- Limit: The merge, accepting an ADR and confirming an intent stay with Ship every change the same way, Manage ADRs and Specify the product.
+- Fails if: A pinned checkpoint of today's plays is missing from the list, or the list and the gate rule's pinned set disagree.
+- Fails if: A pinned yes was skipped by a setting, a policy or an agent.
+- Fails if: The list states an answer to #992's open point before its ADR is accepted.
+
+## Context
+- Read: Gather it from the memory layer. Look first at the project's existing memory and its existing implementation, then Garura memory, then Phoenix memory. If none of them answers, research it and raise a memory update for a person to approve. For this part, look for: each play's checkpoints declared pinned, the gate rule's pinned set and its loop exceptions, how each pinned checkpoint behaves inside a loop, the machine checks before the merge's yes, and #992 with its ADR once it is accepted.
+- Never read: any memory file by its path, and any ICE page.
+- Persona: the product owner, who gives the pinned yeses and wants to know which ones no setting reaches.
+- Scope: In: the list of pinned yeses, why each is pinned, where it is asked, what happens inside a loop, its agreement with the gate rule, and each one's answer once #992's ADR gives it. Out: the merge itself, accepting an ADR, confirming an intent, pinning or unpinning a checkpoint, the settings, and where an owed entry is kept.
+
+## Expectation
+- Scenario: In a clinic's booking app, a reader opens the list before the first merge. It names the merge onto main, confirming an intent and accepting an ADR by hand, the three shaping checkpoints and the three of /edit-ontology, each with why it is pinned and what happens inside a loop, and it names the same set as the gate rule. A team member sets every checkpoint off in the settings; the merge still waits for the product owner's typed yes. Each entry says that the answer to #992's open point is not decided yet.
+- Done means: Someone other than the one who built it compares the list with every checkpoint today's plays declare pinned and with the gate rule, and finds them the same; turns every checkpoint off in the settings and finds each pinned yes still asked; and finds no answer to #992's open point stated before its ADR is accepted.
