+  - Feature to add when this capability is reviewed: a tool that knows how to create and edit the product model (#1030). Not built, and to be built later.
+  - The product owner's answers of 2026-11-11 to the eight questions of the stock-take (.garura/project/issues/1021/context/bi-11-inventory/inventory.md, section 9), his words kept as given: "Yeah, experimentations are only features. There is nothing new. Whether they need to be built as A/B testing or whatnot is something which we can decide later, but those are essentially features." / "No, the team can extend the ontology that Corona provides. It's not linked, but if they do extend it, they would need to go back and change the place as well. Changing the ontology will break the place. It all has to go hand in hand, but it is extendable, which is fine." / "Yes, every ontology should run the model before and after. I don't understand question 4. I'll go with your proposal of no. Apart from being found on its own, no, a feature doesn't need another feature. All of that is managed in the slices." / "Managing the model should hold any checks of the model as well. Managing the model should hold the edits as well. Yes, it should hold ontology as well."
+    - Read as: 1, ideas and experiments are features, nothing new, how they are built (A/B tests or other) decided later; 2, a team can extend the ontology Garura provides, and extending it means changing the plays with it ("Corona" and "the place" read as Garura and the plays); 3, every ontology change runs the model's checks before and after; 4, no (our proposal); 5, no, a feature does not need another feature, that order is managed in the slices; 6, Manage the model holds the model's checks; 7, Manage the model holds the edits; 8, read as yes, the product profile and the product decision become kinds of the ontology, to be confirmed when BI-11 resumes.
+    - He asked that BI-10 is closed first: "Let close BI 10 properly before we go to BI 11."
+    - Asked whether his "Yes, it should hold ontology as well" meant one capability (Manage holds the ontology) or yes to question 8, he wrote on 2026-11-11: "model is implementation of the onology. hence managing ontology is a differnet capability and then managing model is a different capability. what we are doing here is managing the model, and we have some implementation in place while plays are missing, templates are missing etc. and as ontology changes, installing a new version will mean adding freature to upgrade and handle the changes to the model too"
+    - Read as: two capabilities. Define what a product is made of manages the ontology; Manage the model manages the model, the ontology's implementation, with its checks and its edits; the plays and templates it lacks are features of it. Question 8 stays yes (the product profile and the product decision become kinds of the ontology). When the ontology changes, an upgrade moves the model to the new version: Upgrade a project's Move the product model to the new version's shape (fn-move-model, BI-7) is that feature, and Define gives it the model's recorded shape version it lacks.
