+      "fix": ""
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "depth_gradient",
+      "verdict": "pass",
+      "evidence": "\"The work has two steps. The agent writes the typed words into the working file, and then a script makes the copy. Only the second step is mechanical.\"",
+      "fix": ""
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "stranger_test",
+      "verdict": "fail",
+      "evidence": "\"The kept text is the Source, and the run drafts its intents from it.\" \"Given a person who answers a later question, when the answer is recorded, then the kept text's fingerprint has not changed.\"",
+      "fix": "Make the page stand alone. Define in a clause each term it uses but does not explain: 'Source' (the saved copy later steps read, so they need not go back to the original), 'fingerprint' (a short code worked out from the file's bytes, so any change to the text changes the code), 'the run's evidence' and 'the answers record'. Add the why of keeping the words untouched, and one rule for the case where no one is named as the giver, so a cold reader can explain what, why and edges from this page alone."
+    }
+  ]
+}
