+{"citation_id": "cite-20261102-001", "issue": 1021, "play": "reorganise business intents (no play, a run the product owner approved)", "question": "What shape does a capability page take at the directional depth, with no features written?", "answer": "Title, Directional intent, Sources, then the Agent intent (ICE) as the last section. There is no Features heading at this stage, so the page says in a Features line inside its text that none are written yet.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-02T15:51:41Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the required headings of a directional capability page", "found": "the directional stage requires only the title and Directional intent", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/capability.md", "start": 22, "end": 30, "fingerprint": "sha256:56800b4cb943d31c510874807f98a0b96e6bb5d3ea42d38748d5e461cb52d314", "text": "\n```\n# Capability: <Capability Name>\n## Directional intent\n```\n\n- **Directional intent** — what this capability is about, the rough direction of its\n  scope (what it will broadly own), and why it matters to the domain. A substantive\n  paragraph a stranger understands at a directional level — not the full detail, which", "version": "c14f515d910f", "around": {"start": 19, "end": 33, "text": "> scores depth and self-explanation against `_content-standard.md`.\n\n## Heading contract — DIRECTIONAL stage (required, in order) · usually /discover-intent or /discover-domains\n\n```\n# Capability: <Capability Name>\n## Directional intent\n```\n\n- **Directional intent** — what this capability is about, the rough direction of its\n  scope (what it will broadly own), and why it matters to the domain. A substantive\n  paragraph a stranger understands at a directional level — not the full detail, which\n  is /discover-capabilities's job. It must still self-explain (the *why*), not just name the area.\n\n## Heading contract — DETAILED stage (required, in order) · usually /discover-capabilities"}}}, {"asked": "where Sources and the agent intent sit, and what the ICE lines are", "found": "Sources comes after the other sections and before the agent intent; the agent intent is the last section at every stage", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/capability.md", "start": 60, "end": 72, "fingerprint": "sha256:2aece204786a02470e97e815d4990d0f68e8b676289420411c050622544d9010", "text": "- Goal: <what must be true here — one line per goal>\n- Limit: <a line that must not be crossed>\n- Fails if: <what counts as failing>\n- Context: <who it serves, the systems it touches, what is in and out>\n- Checked by: <how a goal is checked>\n- Quality need: <a concrete target, e.g. speed, security, a regime such as PCI>\n```\n\nThe agent's intent for this node (ontology: ICE), in one place an agent can point at.\nEach line starts with one of the six labels; a label may repeat; at least one **Goal**.\nA play fills the lines it knows — a light section has only goals, a full one has every\nlabel — and a later play adds to it, keeping what is there. The section is expected once\nthe node's spine entry names a business intent in `intents` (the node is built from that", "version": "c14f515d910f", "around": {"start": 57, "end": 75, "text": "\n```\n## Agent intent (ICE)\n- Goal: <what must be true here — one line per goal>\n- Limit: <a line that must not be crossed>\n- Fails if: <what counts as failing>\n- Context: <who it serves, the systems it touches, what is in and out>\n- Checked by: <how a goal is checked>\n- Quality need: <a concrete target, e.g. speed, security, a regime such as PCI>\n```\n\nThe agent's intent for this node (ontology: ICE), in one place an agent can point at.\nEach line starts with one of the six labels; a label may repeat; at least one **Goal**.\nA play fills the lines it knows — a light section has only goals, a full one has every\nlabel — and a later play adds to it, keeping what is there. The section is expected once\nthe node's spine entry names a business intent in `intents` (the node is built from that\nintent, so its agent intent should be written); a linked node without it gets a linter\nwarning — alignment work, never a stop — so pages written before ontology v4 still pass.\nA node with no intent link may leave it out."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261102-002", "issue": 1021, "play": "reorganise business intents (no play, a run the product owner approved)", "question": "Where do Sources and the agent intent sit on a directional capability page? (Corrects the line range of the second step of cite-20261102-001.)", "answer": "Sources sits after the other sections and before the agent intent, and the agent intent is the last section at every stage.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-02T15:51:58Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the directional stage's required headings", "found": "the title and Directional intent only", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/capability.md", "start": 22, "end": 25, "fingerprint": "sha256:89800d564ac8fd1ec5b493b3f2859761b87c821e58576f5d4ed59244e86be34f", "text": "\n```\n# Capability: <Capability Name>\n## Directional intent", "version": "c14f515d910f", "around": {"start": 19, "end": 28, "text": "> scores depth and self-explanation against `_content-standard.md`.\n\n## Heading contract — DIRECTIONAL stage (required, in order) · usually /discover-intent or /discover-domains\n\n```\n# Capability: <Capability Name>\n## Directional intent\n```\n\n- **Directional intent** — what this capability is about, the rough direction of its"}}}, {"asked": "where Sources sits", "found": "after the other sections, before the agent intent", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/capability.md", "start": 43, "end": 43, "fingerprint": "sha256:34f6a8ad1c20572b946dbd4b0f3df8925f8a2db1637e0ed13c3dbff118196007", "text": "## Sources — after the other sections, before the agent intent (#689)", "version": "c14f515d910f", "around": {"start": 40, "end": 46, "text": "## Features\n```\n\n## Sources — after the other sections, before the agent intent (#689)\n\n```\n## Sources"}}}, {"asked": "where the agent intent sits", "found": "the last section, at every stage", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/capability.md", "start": 56, "end": 56, "fingerprint": "sha256:38eb69bc9942542a94fbc1dcb697ffaea563be4de6988d204b8537f52693c823", "text": "## Agent intent (ICE) — the last section, at every stage", "version": "c14f515d910f", "around": {"start": 53, "end": 59, "text": "One source per line. A part nothing shows is not written. Optional for older pages; every\nplay that writes the page writes it.\n\n## Agent intent (ICE) — the last section, at every stage\n\n```\n## Agent intent (ICE)"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261103-001", "issue": 1021, "play": "reorganise business intents (no play, a run the product owner approved)", "question": "What shape do the capability page and the feature pages take when they hold only the words the product owner approved?", "answer": "The capability page has its title, Directional intent, then the Agent intent (ICE) last, with one-liner, unique line and Features line inside Directional intent. Each feature page has its title, What it does, then the Agent intent (ICE) last. The other four feature sections are not written, because the approved text holds no words for them.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-03T03:38:48Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the required headings of a directional capability page", "found": "the directional stage requires only the title and Directional intent", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/capability.md", "start": 22, "end": 30, "fingerprint": "sha256:56800b4cb943d31c510874807f98a0b96e6bb5d3ea42d38748d5e461cb52d314", "text": "\n```\n# Capability: <Capability Name>\n## Directional intent\n```\n\n- **Directional intent** — what this capability is about, the rough direction of its\n  scope (what it will broadly own), and why it matters to the domain. A substantive\n  paragraph a stranger understands at a directional level — not the full detail, which", "version": "d8704631a590", "around": {"start": 19, "end": 33, "text": "> scores depth and self-explanation against `_content-standard.md`.\n\n## Heading contract — DIRECTIONAL stage (required, in order) · usually /discover-intent or /discover-domains\n\n```\n# Capability: <Capability Name>\n## Directional intent\n```\n\n- **Directional intent** — what this capability is about, the rough direction of its\n  scope (what it will broadly own), and why it matters to the domain. A substantive\n  paragraph a stranger understands at a directional level — not the full detail, which\n  is /discover-capabilities's job. It must still self-explain (the *why*), not just name the area.\n\n## Heading contract — DETAILED stage (required, in order) · usually /discover-capabilities"}}}, {"asked": "the required headings of a feature page", "found": "a feature page requires What it does, Inputs / Outputs, Rules & behavior, Acceptance criteria and Out of scope, and the linter enforces them", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/feature.md", "start": 10, "end": 20, "fingerprint": "sha256:4e4810e61c16c59cd8a1444a54e59d99a94a7c15ef76bb6311ec5b033b2b8aea", "text": "## Heading contract (required, in order)\n\n```\n# Feature: <Feature Name>\n## What it does\n## Inputs / Outputs\n## Rules & behavior\n## Acceptance criteria\n## Out of scope\n```\n", "version": "d8704631a590", "around": {"start": 7, "end": 23, "text": "> the depth-gradient against `_content-standard.md`. Written by `/discover-capabilities`\n> (and by `/shape-slice` for a feature a slice needs that the model lacks).\n\n## Heading contract (required, in order)\n\n```\n# Feature: <Feature Name>\n## What it does\n## Inputs / Outputs\n## Rules & behavior\n## Acceptance criteria\n## Out of scope\n```\n\n## Per-section guidance\n\n- **What it does** — the function's behavior in concrete terms: when it runs, on"}}}, {"asked": "where the agent intent sits on a feature page and what its lines are", "found": "the agent intent is the last section at every stage, each line starting with one of six labels, with at least one Goal", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/feature.md", "start": 49, "end": 59, "fingerprint": "sha256:eef6438846d30a05f08ec7e55c9531c3eb1de9cb1c5859d8a023060995a9e17e", "text": "```\n## Agent intent (ICE)\n- Goal: <what must be true here — one line per goal>\n- Limit: <a line that must not be crossed>\n- Fails if: <what counts as failing>\n- Context: <who it serves, the systems it touches, what is in and out>\n- Checked by: <how a goal is checked>\n- Quality need: <a concrete target, e.g. speed, security, a regime such as PCI>\n```\n\nThe agent's intent for this node (ontology: ICE), in one place an agent can point at.", "version": "d8704631a590", "around": {"start": 46, "end": 62, "text": "\n## Agent intent (ICE) — the last section, at every stage\n\n```\n## Agent intent (ICE)\n- Goal: <what must be true here — one line per goal>\n- Limit: <a line that must not be crossed>\n- Fails if: <what counts as failing>\n- Context: <who it serves, the systems it touches, what is in and out>\n- Checked by: <how a goal is checked>\n- Quality need: <a concrete target, e.g. speed, security, a regime such as PCI>\n```\n\nThe agent's intent for this node (ontology: ICE), in one place an agent can point at.\nEach line starts with one of the six labels; a label may repeat; at least one **Goal**.\nA play fills the lines it knows — a light section has only goals, a full one has every\nlabel — and a later play adds to it, keeping what is there. The section is expected once"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261106-001", "issue": 1021, "play": "redraft of the judge-failed pages (issue 1021, capability 1)", "question": "How do the redrafted pages explain an ICE to a cold reader?", "answer": "An ICE is the agent's intent for one capability or feature: what an agent must make true there, for whom, and how it is checked.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-06T14:39:22Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what an ICE is, in the ontology", "found": "the ICE kind's 'What it is' line", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/ontology.md", "start": 482, "end": 482, "fingerprint": "sha256:65ac5c62d418e1179143a4b2b7fee4e54793951356ab5fdfcdec5a33367c06db", "text": "**What it is:** The agent's intent for one capability or one feature: what an agent must make true there, for whom, and how it will be checked. It is its own node, with its own page and its own spine entry, and it holds three parts: **Intent** (goals, limits, fails if), **Context** (the rules for the sub-agent that gathers context: what to read, what never to read, the persona, the scope) and **Expectation** (scenarios, done means, quality needs). It has no link to a business intent; it finds its business intents through its part. It is the node that answers \"can work start here?\" with ready, partly ready or not ready. No work item carries it. Two plays read it, each for its own lines: `/shape-slice` reads the \"Fails if\" lines and writes the slice's hidden file from them; the plan play reads every other line of a Feature's ICE and that Feature's Capability's ICE when it makes the Story, and writes the Story's scope of work and Context guidance from them. It can be **thin**: proposed from the person's words by the play that needed it — today `/shape-slice` or `/update-plan` — and marked so. It is not the business intent (the person's intent), and it is not the capability or feature page (that page says what the part is; the ICE says what an agent must make true there). In this ontology, Context is one part of an ICE only — not the run folder of a play.", "version": "b2e40bff2131", "around": {"start": 479, "end": 485, "text": "\n### ICE\n\n**What it is:** The agent's intent for one capability or one feature: what an agent must make true there, for whom, and how it will be checked. It is its own node, with its own page and its own spine entry, and it holds three parts: **Intent** (goals, limits, fails if), **Context** (the rules for the sub-agent that gathers context: what to read, what never to read, the persona, the scope) and **Expectation** (scenarios, done means, quality needs). It has no link to a business intent; it finds its business intents through its part. It is the node that answers \"can work start here?\" with ready, partly ready or not ready. No work item carries it. Two plays read it, each for its own lines: `/shape-slice` reads the \"Fails if\" lines and writes the slice's hidden file from them; the plan play reads every other line of a Feature's ICE and that Feature's Capability's ICE when it makes the Story, and writes the Story's scope of work and Context guidance from them. It can be **thin**: proposed from the person's words by the play that needed it — today `/shape-slice` or `/update-plan` — and marked so. It is not the business intent (the person's intent), and it is not the capability or feature page (that page says what the part is; the ICE says what an agent must make true there). In this ontology, Context is one part of an ICE only — not the run folder of a play.\n**Who reads it:** agent\n**Layer:** product\n**In the tracker as:** none — model only"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261106-002", "issue": 1021, "play": "redraft of the judge-failed pages (issue 1021, capability 1)", "question": "How do the redrafted pages explain the rubric?", "answer": "The rubric is the written rule for what a good ICE looks like; it asks for exactly one Goal, which the structure check does not test.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-06T14:39:22Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what the ICE rubric is", "found": "its opening line", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/rules/ice-rubric.md", "start": 3, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:aea832a380945f352bb8bca1ffb845506a3b8e9bfe41f1084db23629fa114523", "text": "What a good ICE looks like. It holds for every capability and feature, and for a thin ICE as much as a full one. A person, a play or a judge reads an ICE against this table.", "version": "b2e40bff2131", "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "# ICE Rubric\n\nWhat a good ICE looks like. It holds for every capability and feature, and for a thin ICE as much as a full one. A person, a play or a judge reads an ICE against this table.\n\nAn ICE is not a section of a capability or feature page. It has its own page, `ice.md`, in the folder of its part, and its own entry in the model's index. The page has three sections, in this order: Intent, Context and Expectation. The ontology's ICE kind holds the full shape.\n"}}}, {"asked": "a rubric rule the structure check leaves unchecked", "found": "Goal: exactly one", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/rules/ice-rubric.md", "start": 9, "end": 9, "fingerprint": "sha256:558c888c233512830d3a3c44e7b4a1cee83cbf3c5ac57cd01530456acc4dc41a", "text": "| **Intent** | **Goal** | Exactly one. This is not negotiable. Two goals mean two parts: split the part, or move one goal down to a feature. |", "version": "b2e40bff2131", "around": {"start": 6, "end": 12, "text": "\n| Section | Line | Rule |\n|---------|------|------|\n| **Intent** | **Goal** | Exactly one. This is not negotiable. Two goals mean two parts: split the part, or move one goal down to a feature. |\n| | **Limit** | At least one. A thin ICE has up to three. |\n| | **Fails if** | At least one, for what matters most. A thin ICE has up to three. |\n| **Context** | **Read** | Says where the context is gathered from, in the fixed order below, and what to look for. |"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261106-003", "issue": 1021, "play": "redraft of the judge-failed pages (issue 1021, capability 1)", "question": "Why does the model need domains (Specify domains page)?", "answer": "Domains group the product's capabilities into fields the industry knows, at the level a business leader talks about.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-06T14:39:22Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what a domain is, in the ontology", "found": "a big area that groups capabilities", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/ontology.md", "start": 293, "end": 293, "fingerprint": "sha256:80c3c52cd046a2a4e0e7caeeeb24197d00cc11d8c17ec3be94c7392c68afe9b0", "text": "**What it is:** A big area of the product that groups capabilities. Its page is light (directional) or full (detailed); it holds no ICE. It links loosely to business intents, for search only. It is in the model only: it is never in a plan, never stops work, and no work item links to it. It is not a capability (a capability is something the product can do; a domain groups them).", "version": "b2e40bff2131", "around": {"start": 290, "end": 296, "text": "\n### Domain\n\n**What it is:** A big area of the product that groups capabilities. Its page is light (directional) or full (detailed); it holds no ICE. It links loosely to business intents, for search only. It is in the model only: it is never in a plan, never stops work, and no work item links to it. It is not a capability (a capability is something the product can do; a domain groups them).\n**Who reads it:** both\n**Layer:** product\n**In the tracker as:** none — model only"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261106-004", "issue": 1021, "play": "redraft of the judge-failed pages (issue 1021, capability 1)", "question": "Why can a title, an outcome or a limit not be the run's own proposal (Specify intents page)?", "answer": "These three say what the person wants, so each must rest on one of the other bases, not on our own proposal.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-06T14:39:22Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what a business intent is", "found": "what a person wants, in their words", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/ontology.md", "start": 175, "end": 175, "fingerprint": "sha256:dd55836f30a6a7ad11e73a9ebb014ab151be962c875c5fedceb42acc4391e67c", "text": "**What it is:** What a person or the organisation wants, in their words: the outcome as a hypothesis (what should be true, why it matters, and how we will know it is met), the boundaries it must stay inside, the rules it must keep, and the capabilities that serve it. It is the person's interface to the product, and it is for tracking. It holds no ICE, and Garura never works on a business intent directly: agents work on the ICE of its capabilities and of their features. It is not ICE (the agent's intent) and not a work item.", "version": "b2e40bff2131", "around": {"start": 172, "end": 178, "text": "\n### Business Intent\n\n**What it is:** What a person or the organisation wants, in their words: the outcome as a hypothesis (what should be true, why it matters, and how we will know it is met), the boundaries it must stay inside, the rules it must keep, and the capabilities that serve it. It is the person's interface to the product, and it is for tracking. It holds no ICE, and Garura never works on a business intent directly: agents work on the ICE of its capabilities and of their features. It is not ICE (the agent's intent) and not a work item.\n**Who reads it:** person\n**Layer:** product\n**In the tracker as:** an issue labelled `product` — the only kind with that label"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261106-005", "issue": 1021, "play": "redraft of the judge-failed pages (issue 1021, capability 1)", "question": "What is a learned policy and why may it pass a change with no wait (Specify domains page)?", "answer": "A project rule learned from the person's earlier answers; a shape the person approved three times in a row with no edit may pass.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-06T14:39:22Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the conditional gate and its learned policy", "found": "the human's real action teaches the policy", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/rules/gate-config.md", "start": 13, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:ddece0eb8d5ba920642e392c70533b598ed639705379a3182cd0ea1ad9d1f073", "text": "| **conditional** | Fires unless the learned per-project policy says this change SHAPE is auto. Every crossing appends a live-eval line; the human's real action is the verdict that teaches the policy. | The gate policy, learned from the ledger |", "version": "b2e40bff2131", "around": {"start": 10, "end": 16, "text": "| Kind | Meaning | Who decides |\n|---|---|---|\n| **pinned** | Always fires. No config value, policy, or ledger can turn it off. | The play's intent (unpinning = edit-play intent change) |\n| **conditional** | Fires unless the learned per-project policy says this change SHAPE is auto. Every crossing appends a live-eval line; the human's real action is the verdict that teaches the policy. | The gate policy, learned from the ledger |\n| **off** | Never waits. The checkpoint's judgment was replaced by named deterministic checks inside the play's loop; the skip is recorded. | Config (`gates.plays.<play>: off`), granted only in the same change that adds the replacement checks |\n\n## The config block"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261106-006", "issue": 1021, "play": "redraft of the judge-failed pages (issue 1021, capability 1)", "question": "Why is a light domain page raised and kept, never cut back (Specify domains page)?", "answer": "No one play owns a domain page, so each play writes what it knows and a later play raises it.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-06T14:39:22Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who owns a domain page", "found": "no play owns a domain; a later play raises it", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "standards/schemas/product-os/grounding/domain.md", "start": 11, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:2f67fa3db228b26a184f571a8a5ff1e55fad97318ef3a729c5077ae0041268ac", "text": "> one applies via the domain entry's `detail:` field (`directional | detailed`).** No\n> play owns a domain (ontology v3): any play writes the page at the depth of what it\n> knows, and a later play raises it.", "version": "b2e40bff2131", "around": {"start": 8, "end": 16, "text": "> cold.\n>\n> **This doc is STAGE-AWARE — it has two valid shapes, and the spine records which\n> one applies via the domain entry's `detail:` field (`directional | detailed`).** No\n> play owns a domain (ontology v3): any play writes the page at the depth of what it\n> knows, and a later play raises it.\n>\n> - **directional** — a light page: what the domain is for, when that is all a play\n>   knows yet (for example `/discover-intent`, reading a prototype)."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261107-001", "issue": 1021, "play": "reorganise business intents (#1021), capability 3 write", "question": "How many lines does BI-1's Touches list gain for the parts of capabilities 2 and 3?", "answer": "11: Turn intents into agent work and its 4 features (5 lines), and Keep the spec matched to what's built and its 5 features (6 lines). The brief said 10; the parts it named, and the approved write plan, come to 11.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-11-07T11:34:15Z", "trace": [{"asked": "which parts BI-1's touched list gains in the approved write plan", "found": "BI-1's touched parts gain the parts of capabilities 2 and 3", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "1021/context/capability-3/page-approvals.md", "start": 11, "end": 11, "fingerprint": "sha256:0b65fc894c3cb1e06ec29a1bfa7187880ec7ebf5fefdbcf1cb67ea2b24364b19", "text": "- 2026-11-07, page 6 of 6, Find where the spec and what's built no longer match, page and its ICE page, thin mark. The product owner replied: \"approved\", also approving the write plan: 12 pages, 6 parts and 6 ICE entries; BI-1's touched parts gain the parts of capabilities 2 and 3; Specify the product's \"no capability owns it yet\" line points here; #977 moves under BI-1.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 11, "text": "- 2026-11-07, page 3 of 6, Keep an intent's links current, page and its ICE page, no thin mark. The product owner replied: \"approved\". The question whether an intent page may list features was not answered, so it stays \"Not decided\" on the page.\n- 2026-11-07, page 4 of 6, Replace or retire an intent, page and its ICE page, no thin mark. The product owner replied: \"approved\".\n- 2026-11-07, page 5 of 6, Keep the tracker's words matched to the model, page and its ICE page, no thin mark. The product owner replied: \"approved\".\n- 2026-11-07, page 6 of 6, Find where the spec and what's built no longer match, page and its ICE page, thin mark. The product owner replied: \"approved\", also approving the write plan: 12 pages, 6 parts and 6 ICE entries; BI-1's touched parts gain the parts of capabilities 2 and 3; Specify the product's \"no capability owns it yet\" line points here; #977 moves under BI-1."}}}], "from_update": null}
